config DT_RECONFIGURABLE
	bool "Runtime-reconfigurable devicetree resources"
	help
	  Enable a RAM-backed descriptor table for devicetree nodes marked with
	  the "zephyr,reconfigurable" property. Each descriptor is seeded from the
	  node's devicetree reg/interrupts and may be patched at runtime from a
	  manifest (for example on an FPGA dynamic-function-exchange segment switch)
	  before the owning device is (re)initialized. This provides dynamic
	  devicetree resource handling without a runtime flattened devicetree (FDT)
	  blob on the target. Descriptors are created with DT_RECONFIGURABLE_DEFINE().
